Highlights:
1. Hollow MOFs were first applied into seawater uranium extraction.
2. Uranium could be efficiently extracted from aqueous solution by DAMN functionalized double-shelled MIL-101 material.
3. The maximum adsorption capacity is $601\mathrm{~mg~g^{-1}}$ , exceeding all known amino groups grafted onto MIL-101 adsorbents.
4. Hollow properties play a key role in the adsorption of materials.
5. The adsorbent shows high selectivity and great adsorption rate in simulated seawater.
